","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-07-18T12:14:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T04:58:29Z","closed_at":"2026-07-19T04:58:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\ntested/found in: Godot 4.7.1 Stable\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 970 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-2400 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads) - 19.95 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nthe map is a single mesh\n\nNot All reflection probes in my Compitability renderer Scene (i have 4 Probes) work, only 2 or 1, probes that dont work briefly work when project starts but then just disappear as if theres a limit on ReflectionProbes i'm not aware of\n\nframe 1:\n\n<img width=\"1010\" height=\"568\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b540f3d4-5186-4e5b-9224-23146d142654\" />\n\nseveral frames after:\n\n<img width=\"1006\" height=\"564\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/742f48df-0138-4249-83a9-056e9b825251\" />\n\n\n\nIf i will try to set non-working Probe to *update: Always*, the mesh that is inside of that probe may disappear under certain angles, does not happen in *update: once* \n\n<img width=\"1150\" height=\"649\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0539a14b-a2b9-483d-a567-3389bd9a0906\" />\n\n\n\n*please dont assasinate me for this \"report\", i should probably have asked community first. but maybe this is an actual bug with amount of probes that can interact with a single mesh*\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ntrying to reproduce, problem does not seem to presist in basic scenes (or now i think that the reason is the fact that i use a single mesh for my map)\n\n<img width=\"913\" height=\"472\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/133c302f-3389-47e1-977b-0e22aed39904\" />\n\nit does in an empty scene with my level's mesh tho\n\n<img width=\"1155\" height=\"645\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a10c1750-0381-4220-b0dc-a8daebc540c0\" />\n\ntheres a probe on the asphalt and a probe in the elevator, and none of them seem to work, but the third probe works\n\n<img width=\"1156\" height=\"646\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/39a99a87-75b6-4d30-9c24-0f2c2892ad0f\" />\n\ni don't know if this is a bug with godot's compitability reflections, the fact that i use a **single mesh** for my entire level, or there is a limit on active probes in compitability\n\n<img width=\"556\" height=\"138\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da2212be-69ab-4d7b-85c6-688f56247179\" />\n\nReflection Atlas:\n\n- Reflection Size: 1024\n- Reflection Size.Mobile: default\n- Reflection Amount: 64, Increacing the amount dosent help\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[repr.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30150646/repr.zip)\n\nstart the project, use spacebar to switch between 3 cameras\n\nnotice how some reflections disappear after new ones are ready? but it seems like only on the level's mesh","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gith